+### Live line pass in progress
+
+The physical world now accepts replaceable CPU road, sea-lane and border buffers;
+their z input is clearance above the presented surface. The tile owner returns
+changed presented domains so distant line heights are not queried or uploaded.
+Border geometry is extracted from the raw GPU pass into its CPU owner, consumed
+by both paths. Existing composition, fog and DPR1/DPR2 anchor snapshots stayed
+pixel-identical in the first merged browser pass; all498 CPU tests passed.
+
+Actual Italy/Alps captures exposed long border triangles dipping through hills.
+The initial captures are retained under `assets/slice-11/lines/rejected-sparse`.
+The next candidate subdivides border strips along and across their width before
+seating, preserving the existing centerline, colors and clearance. Its focused
+ridge test passes; full visual repeat and fresh critique are still pending.
+Full-region storage/culling and UI/scenery performance remain open.
